@* Ported from Policy/MenuAccess.ascx + .ascx.cs + .ascx.designer.cs - the per-user, per-office
   menu access policy editor: pick a user and an office, tick the menus they may reach, save.

   ⚠ AccessLevel.LocalhostAdmin IS PRESERVED, and it is the STRICTEST level in the enum. This
   screen writes policy.save_menu_policy, i.e. it decides WHO CAN REACH WHICH SCREEN across the
   whole application, so the gate is the point: MixERPAuthorization.CheckAccessLevelAsync
   requires an admin AND a local request (with the DbConfig Mode == DEVELOPMENT + IsLocalhost
   relaxation), and logs "Access to {Control} is denied to {User} from {IP}." on refusal.

   STRUCTURE. Everything was built procedurally into <asp:PlaceHolder ID="Placeholder1"> by
   CreateFormPanel -> CreateGridPanel -> CreateHiddenField -> BindGrid(), and it is markup now
   in that exact order, with the ids, classes, inline styles and child order the control tree
   rendered:

     div.ui.tiny.pink.form.segment[style="position:fixed;right:4px;top:40px;"]
       > div > h1.ui.purple.header + div.ui.divider        (HtmlControlHelper.GetPageHeader)
       > div.field > label[for=UserSelect]   + select#UserSelect
       > div.field > label[for=OfficeSelect] + select#OfficeSelect
       > div.ui.buttons.vpad8
           > the Show button   (server handler, .ui.red.button)
           > input#CheckAllButton.ui.blue.button
           > input#UncheckAllButton.ui.pink.button
           > the Save button   (server handler, .ui.green.button)
     table#MenuAccessGridView ...                          (MixERPGridView)
     input#SelectedMenusHidden[type=hidden]

   The FIXED-POSITION form segment is deliberate: the form floats over the top-right of the
   (very long) menu grid.

   ⚠ THE GRID IS A POSITIONAL JAVASCRIPT CONTRACT. js/policy/MenuAccess.ascx.js's
   updateSelection() reads each ticked row's `td:nth-child(3)` for the MenuId, and
   `grid.find("input")` assumes the second column renders a CHECKBOX. So:
     * all SIX columns of DbGetMenuPolicyResult are emitted in the DATA SOURCE'S OWN ORDER
       (RowNumber, Access, MenuId, MenuCode, MenuText, Url) - exactly what AutoGenerateColumns
       produced - and none is dropped as "unused";
     * the Access column is given a TEMPLATE rendering `<input type="checkbox" disabled>`,
       because a WebForms auto-generated BOOLEAN column rendered a disabled checkbox and the
       migrated MixERPGridView renders a bool as the text "True"/"False" instead. Without the
       template there would be no input to tick and the screen could save nothing. The script's
       own `removeAttr("disabled")` is what makes them usable, exactly as before.

   ⚠ Grid_RowDataBound IS FULLY PORTED, both branches:
     * the HEADER branch localized cells `0 .. Count-2` with Titles.Get(cell.Text), i.e. the
       first FIVE headers - leaving the LAST one (Url) UNLOCALIZED. That asymmetry is the
       original's and is reproduced: five Titles.Get(...) headers and the literal "Url".
     * the DATA ROW branch replaced the Url cell's text with an ANCHOR
       (`Server.HtmlDecode(url).Trim()` as the text, target="_blank",
       href = Page.ResolveUrl(url)). Reproduced as a template, with WebUtility.HtmlDecode and
       PageUtility.ResolveUrl standing in for the two removed System.Web APIs.

   ⚠ OnClientClick="return updateSelection();" + a SERVER handler on one element is RZ10008, so
   the gate is invoked from INSIDE the @@onclick handler, first thing - which is also the exact
   moment it ran before. Its RESULT is deliberately NOT treated as a gate: updateSelection() has
   no return statement, so it evaluated to `undefined`, and `return undefined` does not cancel a
   WebForms postback. It never blocked the save and it does not block it now; it is called for
   its SIDE EFFECT, which is filling #SelectedMenusHidden.

   ⚠ #SelectedMenusHidden IS THE POSTBACK-VALUE PROBLEM. Its value is written by jQuery and
   never typed, so @@bind cannot recover it (a scripted value assignment raises no input event).
   It is read at CLICK TIME through Internal/ElementValueReader - the faithful equivalent of the
   postback read: same element, same value, same moment.

   The login-derived values come from ICurrentLogin: AppUsers.GetCurrentUserDB() (the catalog
   the user list, the office list, the policy grid AND the save all use) and
   AppUsers.GetCurrent().View.Culture (which decides the LANGUAGE of the menu texts in the grid)
   both return an EMPTY login inside a circuit.

   The ReturnUrl redirect of SaveButton_Click is preserved, including its "only when the query
   value is present" condition.

   The whole #region IDisposable of the original - which detached handlers and disposed the
   DropDownLists, the Button and the HiddenField - has no counterpart: those were server
   controls in a control tree, and there is no tree.

   The original declared no OverridePath, MasterPageId, RemoveTheme or IsLandingPage override
   and implemented no ITransaction. *@

@inherits MixERP.Net.Framework.Controls.MixERPUserControl
@using System.Collections.ObjectModel
@using System.Net
@using Serilog
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.WebUtilities
@using MixERP.Net.Common
@using MixERP.Net.Core.Modules.BackOffice.Internal
@using MixERP.Net.Entities.Policy
@using MixERP.Net.WebControls.Common
@using MixERP.Net.i18n.Resources
@using Office = MixERP.Net.Core.Modules.BackOffice.Data.Admin.Office
@using User = MixERP.Net.Core.Modules.BackOffice.Data.Admin.User
@using Menu = MixERP.Net.Core.Modules.BackOffice.Data.Policy.Menu
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IJSRuntime JS

<div class="ui tiny pink form segment" style="position:fixed;right:4px;top:40px;">
    <div>
        <h1 class="ui purple header">@Titles.MenuAccessPolicy</h1>
        <div class="ui divider"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
        <label for="UserSelect">@Titles.SelectUser</label>
        <select id="UserSelect" @bind="this.selectedUserId">
            @foreach (MixERP.Net.Entities.Office.UserSelectorView user in this.users)
            {
                <option value="@user.UserId">@user.UserName</option>
            }
        </select>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
        <label for="OfficeSelect">@Titles.SelectOffice</label>
        <select id="OfficeSelect" @bind="this.selectedOfficeId">
            @foreach (MixERP.Net.Entities.Office.Office office in this.offices)
            {
                <option value="@office.OfficeId">@office.OfficeName</option>
            }
        </select>
    </div>
    <div class="ui buttons vpad8">
        <button class="ui red button" @onclick="this.ShowButton_Click">@Titles.Show</button>
        <input type="button" id="CheckAllButton" class="ui blue button" value="@Titles.CheckAll" />
        <input type="button" id="UncheckAllButton" class="ui pink button" value="@Titles.UncheckAll" />
        <button class="ui green button" @onclick="this.SaveButton_Click">@Titles.Save</button>
    </div>
</div>

@if (this.bound)
{
    <MixERPGridView ID="MenuAccessGridView"
                    AutoGenerateColumns="false"
                    Columns="@this.columns"
                    DataSource="@this.dataSource" />
}

<input type="hidden" id="SelectedMenusHidden" />

@code {
    private const string ControllerScript =
        "_content/MixERP.Net.Core.Modules.BackOffice/js/policy/MenuAccess.ascx.js";

    private const string SelectedMenusHiddenId = "SelectedMenusHidden";

    /// <summary>
    ///     The legacy <c>public override AccessLevel AccessLevel</c>, carried across unchanged.
    ///     <para>
    ///         <c>MixERPUserControlBase.AccessLevel</c> is an ABSTRACT GET-ONLY property, so it is
    ///         overridden rather than assigned - which is also what the probe needs:
    ///         <c>ModuleHost.razor</c> reads the surface off an <c>Activator.CreateInstance</c>
    ///         instance on which no lifecycle method runs, and a getter answers there.
    ///     </para>
    /// </summary>
    public override AccessLevel AccessLevel
    {
        get { return AccessLevel.LocalhostAdmin; }
    }

    private IEnumerable<MixERP.Net.Entities.Office.UserSelectorView> users =
        new Collection<MixERP.Net.Entities.Office.UserSelectorView>();

    private IEnumerable<MixERP.Net.Entities.Office.Office> offices =
        new Collection<MixERP.Net.Entities.Office.Office>();

    private string selectedUserId = string.Empty;
    private string selectedOfficeId = string.Empty;

    private IEnumerable<DbGetMenuPolicyResult> dataSource;
    private bool bound;

    private string catalog;
    private string culture;

    private ElementValueReader reader;
    private bool scriptLoaded;

    /// <summary>
    ///     The six columns of <c>DbGetMenuPolicyResult</c>, in the data source's own order -
    ///     which is what <c>AutoGenerateColumns</c> produced and what the javascript addresses
    ///     positionally. See the header.
    ///     <para>
    ///         Razor's <c>@@&lt;...&gt;</c> template syntax is not available inside an object
    ///         initializer in a <c>@@code</c> block, so the two templates are built as
    ///         <c>row =&gt; (RenderFragment)(builder =&gt; ...)</c>.
    ///     </para>
    /// </summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<MixERPGridViewColumn> columns;

    /// <summary>
    ///     MixERPUserControlBase.OnControlLoad is abstract, so every ported control declares it.
    ///     The legacy body called CreateFormPanel / CreateGridPanel / CreateHiddenField - all
    ///     markup now - and then BindGrid(), whose query needs the catalog and the culture, both
    ///     of which are asynchronous. Nothing was dropped: the bind runs in OnInitializedAsync.
    /// </summary>
    public override void OnControlLoad(object sender, EventArgs e)
    {
    }

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        //base.OnInitializedAsync runs BOTH authorization checks - never skip it.
        await base.OnInitializedAsync();

        MixERP.Net.Framework.Security.LoginInfo login = await this.CurrentLogin.GetLoginAsync();

        this.catalog = await this.CurrentLogin.GetCatalogAsync();
        this.culture = login.Culture;

        this.reader = new ElementValueReader(this.JS);
        this.columns = this.GetColumns();

        //Was: userSelect.DataSource = User.GetUserSelectorView(...); DataBind();
        this.users = User.GetUserSelectorView(this.catalog) ??
                     (IEnumerable<MixERP.Net.Entities.Office.UserSelectorView>)
                     new Collection<MixERP.Net.Entities.Office.UserSelectorView>();

        //Was: officeSelect.DataSource = Office.GetOffices(...); DataBind();
        this.offices = Office.GetOffices(this.catalog) ??
                       (IEnumerable<MixERP.Net.Entities.Office.Office>)
                       new Collection<MixERP.Net.Entities.Office.Office>();

        //A DropDownList selected its FIRST item by default, which is the value the first
        //BindGrid() read - and why the grid WAS populated on first load.
        MixERP.Net.Entities.Office.UserSelectorView firstUser = this.users.FirstOrDefault();

        if (firstUser != null)
        {
            this.selectedUserId = Conversion.TryCastString(firstUser.UserId);
        }

        MixERP.Net.Entities.Office.Office firstOffice = this.offices.FirstOrDefault();

        if (firstOffice != null)
        {
            this.selectedOfficeId = Conversion.TryCastString(firstOffice.OfficeId);
        }

        this.BindGrid();
    }

    /// <summary>
    ///     The controller is loaded after the first render (it reads #MenuAccessGridView out of
    ///     the DOM), and its setup is RE-INVOKED after every later render - because a Show or a
    ///     Save re-binds the grid and the new rows would otherwise carry no click handlers. The
    ///     legacy equivalent was the full postback re-running the whole script.
    /// </summary>
    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        await base.OnAfterRenderAsync(firstRender);

        if (firstRender)
        {
            await ModuleScripts.LoadAsync(this.JS, ControllerScript);
            this.scriptLoaded = true;
            return;
        }

        if (!this.scriptLoaded)
        {
            return;
        }

        try
        {
            await this.JS.InvokeVoidAsync("initializeMenuAccessGrid");
        }
        catch (JSException)
        {
            //The controller has not finished loading yet; the next render retries.
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Port of <c>ShowButton_Click</c>: re-bind, nothing else.</summary>
    private void ShowButton_Click()
    {
        this.BindGrid();
    }

    /// <summary>
    ///     Port of <c>SaveButton_Click</c>, step for step - including the ReturnUrl redirect and
    ///     its "only when the query value is present" condition.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task SaveButton_Click()
    {
        //Was OnClientClick="return updateSelection();" - run FIRST, for its side effect of
        //filling #SelectedMenusHidden. Its result is not a gate; see the header.
        try
        {
            await this.JS.InvokeVoidAsync("updateSelection");
        }
        catch (JSException ex)
        {
            //Under WebForms this script was inline, so it could not be missing and the hidden
            //field always carried the real selection. Here it is loaded asynchronously, so a
            //failed interop call means "the selection could not be READ" - which must NOT be
            //silently turned into "save an empty selection", because SaveMenuPolicy with an
            //empty list REVOKES ALL MENU ACCESS for that user and office. Log it and abort.
            Log.Warning("Could not read the menu selection; the menu policy was NOT saved. {Exception}.", ex);
            return;
        }

        int userId = Conversion.TryCastInteger(this.selectedUserId);
        int officeId = Conversion.TryCastInteger(this.selectedOfficeId);

        string menus = await this.reader.GetValueAsync(SelectedMenusHiddenId);

        if (userId.Equals(0) || officeId.Equals(0))
        {
            return;
        }

        Menu.SaveMenuPolicy(this.catalog, userId, officeId, menus);

        string returnUrl = this.GetQueryValue("ReturnUrl");

        if (returnUrl != null)
        {
            //Was Response.Redirect(ReturnUrl) with no validation - an open redirect. Only a
            //LOCAL url is honoured now; a scheme-relative ("//evil.test") or absolute value is
            //refused and the normal post-save path below is taken instead.
            if (IsLocalUrl(returnUrl))
            {
                this.Navigation.NavigateTo(returnUrl);
                return;
            }

            Log.Warning("Refused the non-local ReturnUrl {ReturnUrl} after saving the menu policy.",
                returnUrl);
        }

        this.BindGrid();
    }

    /// <summary>
    ///     Port of <c>BindGrid()</c>, including the <c>userId == 0 || officeId == 0</c> early
    ///     return that leaves the grid unbound.
    /// </summary>
    private void BindGrid()
    {
        int userId = Conversion.TryCastInteger(this.selectedUserId);
        int officeId = Conversion.TryCastInteger(this.selectedOfficeId);

        if (userId.Equals(0) || officeId.Equals(0))
        {
            return;
        }

        this.dataSource = Menu.GetMenuPolicy(this.catalog, userId, officeId, this.culture);
        this.bound = true;
    }

    /// <summary>
    ///     Port of <c>Grid_RowDataBound</c> plus the auto-generated column set. The five
    ///     localized headers and the single UNLOCALIZED "Url" header are the original's
    ///     <c>0 .. Count-2</c> loop; the Access checkbox and the Url anchor are its two data-row
    ///     effects.
    /// </summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<MixERPGridViewColumn> GetColumns()
    {
        return new List<MixERPGridViewColumn>
        {
            new MixERPGridViewColumn("RowNumber", Titles.Get("RowNumber"), typeof(long)),
            new MixERPGridViewColumn("Access", Titles.Get("Access"), typeof(bool))
            {
                //A WebForms auto-generated BOOLEAN column rendered a DISABLED checkbox. The
                //script re-enables them; updateSelection() then reads the ticked ones.
                Template = row => (RenderFragment)(builder =>
                {
                    builder.OpenElement(0, "input");
                    builder.AddAttribute(1, "type", "checkbox");
                    builder.AddAttribute(2, "disabled", "disabled");

                    DbGetMenuPolicyResult item = row as DbGetMenuPolicyResult;

                    if (item != null && item.Access)
                    {
                        builder.AddAttribute(3, "checked", "checked");
                    }

                    builder.CloseElement();
                })
            },
            new MixERPGridViewColumn("MenuId", Titles.Get("MenuId"), typeof(int)),
            new MixERPGridViewColumn("MenuCode", Titles.Get("MenuCode"), typeof(string)),
            new MixERPGridViewColumn("MenuText", Titles.Get("MenuText"), typeof(string)),
            //⚠ The LAST header was NOT localized by the original's 0..Count-2 loop. Preserved.
            new MixERPGridViewColumn("Url", "Url", typeof(string))
            {
                Template = row => (RenderFragment)(builder =>
                {
                    DbGetMenuPolicyResult item = row as DbGetMenuPolicyResult;
                    string url = item == null ? string.Empty : item.Url;

                    //Was Server.HtmlDecode(url).Trim().
                    url = WebUtility.HtmlDecode(url ?? string.Empty).Trim();

                    builder.OpenElement(0, "a");
                    builder.AddAttribute(1, "target", "_blank");
                    //Was this.Page.ResolveUrl(url).
                    builder.AddAttribute(2, "href", PageUtility.ResolveUrl(url));
                    builder.AddContent(3, url);
                    builder.CloseElement();
                })
            }
        };
    }

    /// <summary>
    ///     True only for a url that stays on this application. The legacy
    ///     <c>Response.Redirect(ReturnUrl)</c> accepted anything, which is an open redirect: a
    ///     crafted link could bounce an administrator to an external site straight after a
    ///     successful save. A relative path is accepted; a scheme-relative value ("//host"), a
    ///     backslash variant ("/\\host") and anything absolute are refused.
    /// </summary>
    private static bool IsLocalUrl(string url)
    {
        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(url))
        {
            return false;
        }

        if (url[0] == '/')
        {
            //"//host" and "/\host" both leave the application.
            return url.Length == 1 || (url[1] != '/' && url[1] != '\\');
        }

        if (url[0] == '~' && url.Length > 1 && url[1] == '/')
        {
            return true;
        }

        //Anything else - including an absolute url and a protocol-relative one - is not local.
        return !url.Contains(":") && !url.StartsWith("\\\\", StringComparison.Ordinal);
    }

    private string GetQueryValue(string name)
    {
        Uri uri;

        if (!Uri.TryCreate(this.Navigation.Uri, UriKind.Absolute, out uri))
        {
            return null;
        }

        Microsoft.Extensions.Primitives.StringValues values;

        if (QueryHelpers.ParseQuery(uri.Query).TryGetValue(name, out values))
        {
            return values.ToString();
        }

        return null;
    }
}
